a. video group can access /dev/video*. Android media server belongs to arc-camera group. ARC camera service runs as arc-camera user, which belongs to arc-camera group and video group. So media server and ARC camera service can use the socket in /var/run/camera to do IPC. Only ARC camera service can access the camera device.  BUG=b:26311820 TEST=Verify on device that arc-camera has been added to /etc/{passwd,group} and video group has arc-camera as a member. CQ-DEPEND=CL:320853 Change-Id: I8480197e790094b78cfa2a43deb8ca0b9d1e49f7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320067 Commit-Ready: Sheng-hao Tsao &lt;shenghao@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Sheng-hao Tsao &lt;shenghao@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wu-cheng Li &lt;wuchengli@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="320067" owner_email="shenghao@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" ref="refs/changes/67/320067/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0cf4f4c6da0f3d28a9fee3dbaa51882c48734274" commit="82f6509184099427daca4476d49aae27180dd723" commit_message="audio_thread_log_viewer: Disable some grids by checkbox  Add checkboxes for device, stream, fetch, and wake. User can click these checkboxes to disable/enable the grid shown for these events.  BUG=chromium:572816 TEST=click checkbox to disable/enable event grids.  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I0cf4f4c6da0f3d28a9fee3dbaa51882c48734274 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320880 Reviewed-by: Chinyue Chen &lt;chinyue@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320880" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/80/320880/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I02f29ab738acc72e22cd373c5654ebae39cc1aba" commit="8172efc4e559869665df6c702aacae984c928716" commit_message="audio_thread_log_viewer: Change the grid color and log div size  Makes it easier to see the grid text. Also, enlarge the log div so user does not need to scroll too much.  BUG=chromium:572816 TEST=check the html file.  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I02f29ab738acc72e22cd373c5654ebae39cc1aba Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320881 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chinyue Chen &lt;chinyue@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320881" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/81/320881/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic35bbc4bac40823c9ba6add1ecf0b51451593b62" commit="674ab5866ca5d0718fcf9c0729fe5164f3a21ad6" commit_message="gooftool: Remove DUT API.  Gooftool, as a command line program dedicated for &quot;Running locally on a ChromeOS device&quot;, should do everything on its own with restricted dependency and not using remote DUT API.  In station-based mode, gooftool will be executed by being pushed into device in a bundled archive &quot;factory.par&quot; and then executed locally, so we don't need to migrate all the complicated probing code.  There are also some side effects:  - Modem probing is removed because new Chromebooks don't support that.  - dut.info.allowed_channel is removed because no one should override    it, and the only one who reads it is gooftool.  The dependency tree of gooftool after this change is still loading whole test framework due to hwid_utils and its call to shopfloor, which will be revised in other changes.  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: Ic35bbc4bac40823c9ba6add1ecf0b51451593b62 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320455 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320455" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/55/320455/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6e80151130eb2c4b870a84933a9f45f34e118e02" commit="69e959b51a793943a57e6686ddd5f5a5cfc2d656" commit_message="hwid: Reduce dependency to cros.factory.test.  HWID, as the standalone tool, should not rely on the complicated modules in cros.factory.test. In this change we have reduced most of the dependency calls by:  - Change the deprecated cros.factory.test.utils calls to right place.  - Move the call to shopfloor from hwid_utils into hwid_cmdline (the    real place that calls it). Also change GetDeviceInfo to only take    file input.  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I6e80151130eb2c4b870a84933a9f45f34e118e02 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320456 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320456" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/56/320456/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I03ec9fecdd4d857d2552584f424cb707131378ba" commit="0766ab6c140564c42ebe92d2b1303c5005cdbd7c" commit_message="CRAS: iodev_list: Enable fallback device before disabling the only device  In cras_iodev_list_disable_dev, if the device to be disabled is the only enabled device, we should enable fallback device first. This call happens when a node is unplugged. Without this patch, the fallback device will be added some time later after original device is removed. Although this is a small time window, we should enable fallback device first to minimize the time window where there is no device to play data. On Samus this time window is about 5 ms, so this is not actually noticeable to users.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49101 TEST=plug/unplug 3.5mm jack, check audio thread log, see device 2 (fallback device) is enabled before device 8 is disabled. $ grep -E 'DEV_ADDED|DEV_REMOVED' log      70091.549208479  DEV_ADDED                      dev:2      70091.549339569  DEV_REMOVED                    dev:8      70091.675618425  DEV_ADDED                      dev:8      70091.675928957  DEV_REMOVED                    dev:2  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I03ec9fecdd4d857d2552584f424cb707131378ba Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320672 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320672" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/72/320672/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I76307d89c833148ec91c1920630b63af54b47e79" commit="06a5abf32ab4bd9566033043aa5776997c181bde" commit_message="Revert &quot;CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: wait gpu idle instead of set idle time&quot;  This reverts commit 5abdbdf2d3979f5d26cdc066fd679e3b5e3cca7d.  This patch causes GPU hangs. IMG reported that on previous MTK projects, setting SYS_RGX_ACTIVE_POWER_LATENCY_MS to 0 caused system instability.  Let's revert this patch for now while IMG &amp; MTK investigate.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurt@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45713 BUG=chrome-os-partner:49174 TEST=On oak-rev4, load webgl aquarium   =&gt; No &quot;Rats!&quot; WebGL crash messages.  Change-Id: I76307d89c833148ec91c1920630b63af54b47e79 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321231 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321231" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/31/321231/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I35378d8a0c11799ddfa5188c9d9215b532e47352" commit="a0bdd08e765de793e0fd785251ddb6bef947f596" commit_message="Handling probing from goofy UI when DUT is not connected.  Currently goofy UI will try to probe DUT status. When there is no dut connected, lots of error messages will be generated in log and the UI console. Fix those error messages by checking the dut connection first.  BUG=None TEST=Run ryu factory toolkit  Change-Id: I35378d8a0c11799ddfa5188c9d9215b532e47352 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321230 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321230" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/30/321230/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I84a29c6c181b931b7cc00505b99e9ccd0862ae4c" commit="ea14edcad26105ae67eb977f37823134b525c1e3" commit_message="tools: Fix dependency for cros.factory.test.dut.  The cros.factory.test.dut includes DUTBoard, which imports all components and their dependency, which are not required. This change tries to minimize module dependency by moving CalledProcessError to DUTComponent and let DUTBoard use it.  In the meantime, the new dependencies introduced by bluetooth - gtk-2.0 and dbus-gtk bindings, are now added into the known dependency of framework.  BUG=none TEST=make test; py/tools/deps.conf py/test/dut/*.py  Change-Id: I84a29c6c181b931b7cc00505b99e9ccd0862ae4c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321012 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321012" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/12/321012/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I909e5b2ee7b254e0833a905bff70f29d3984ad96" commit="1bcbaf56db12c3637268949bfde40a685ad440c7" commit_message="BACKPORT: ALSA: hda - Move hda_i915.c from sound/pci/hda to sound/hda  The file is moved to hda core and renamed to hdac_i915.c, so can be used by both legacy HDA driver and new Skylake audio driver.  - Add snd_hdac_ prefix to the public APIs. - The i915 audio component is moved to core bus and dynamically allocated. - A static pointer hdac_acomp is used to help bind/unbind callbacks to get   this component, because the sound card's private_data is used by the azx   chip pointer, which is a legacy structure. It could be removed if private   _data changes to some core structure which can be extended to find the   bus. - snd_hdac_get_display_clk() is added to get the display core clock for   HSW/BDW. - haswell_set_bclk() is moved to hda_intel.c because it needs to write the   controller registers EM4/EM5, and only legacy HD-A needs it for HSW/BDW. - Move definition of HSW/BDW-specific registers EM4/EM5 to hda_register.h   and rename them to HSW_EM4/HSW_EM5, because other HD-A controllers have   different layout for the extended mode registers.  Signed-off-by: Mengdong Lin &lt;mengdong.lin@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai &lt;tiwai@suse.de&gt; Link: git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/broonie/sound.git br: for-next (cherry picked from commit 98d8fc6c5d3652e91c61d78941e0fa6f94771d67) Signed-off-by: Vedang Patel &lt;vedang.patel@intel.com&gt;  Conflicts:  (minor context delta in all files.)  sound/hda/Kconfig  sound/pci/hda/hda_i915.c  sound/pci/hda/hda_intel.c  sound/pci/hda/hda_intel.h  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48269 TEST=with the whole series applied, audio works on SKL. TEST=there are no regressions observed on BSW.  Change-Id: I909e5b2ee7b254e0833a905bff70f29d3984ad96 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316161 Commit-Ready: Radhakrishna Sripada &lt;radhakrishna.sripada@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Prathyushi Nangia &lt;prathyushi.nangia@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="316161" owner_email="vedang.patel@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/61/316161/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="7817.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>